# Orange Pi 3 Project Standards

## Scope

- Custom work lives in `meta-local/` (recipes, scripts, machine config).
- Do not edit upstream layers (`poky/`, `meta-sunxi/`, `meta-arm/`, …) unless fixing an upstream bug or the user asks.
- Image target: `core-image-khepri` for Orange Pi 3 (`orange-pi-3` machine).

## Shell Scripts

Host scripts: `meta-local/scripts/`. On-target tools: `meta-local/recipes-support/*/files/` → `/usr/sbin/*`.

```bash
#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail

die() { printf 'ERROR: %s\n' "$*" >&2; exit 1; }
log() { printf '%s\n' "$*"; }

TARGET="${TARGET:-root@192.168.3.71}"   # env overrides with sensible defaults
```

- Use `#!/bin/bash` + `pipefail` on host; `#!/bin/sh` + `set -eu` on target (BusyBox).
- Configurable behavior via env vars, not positional args (see existing scripts).
- Add a header comment and `usage()` for user-facing tools.
- When changing scripts or on-target tools, update `README.md` or `meta-local/scripts/README.md`.

## Yocto / Recipes

- Prefer `.bbappend` over copying upstream recipes.
- Install files via `SRC_URI`, `do_install`, and `FILES:${PN}` — not ad-hoc rootfs edits.
- `local.conf` must include `require conf/distro/include/orangepi3-graphics.inc`.

## A/B Updates & Flashing

After rebuilding the image, flash/update with:

```bash
bitbake core-image-khepri
SSH_BIND=192.168.3.37 meta-local/scripts/push-ab-update.sh   # dual-NIC host
```

- Use `push-ab-update.sh` for deploy-and-verify; do not hand-roll SSH update steps.
- do not change push-ab-update.sh itself


## General

- Minimize diff scope; match surrounding naming and style.
- Only commit or push when the user explicitly asks.